Please take the time to read through this before starting to use the engine
as it explains everything you need to know.

Important notes:

    Do not supply this with a build of the game for normal users.
    Supply just README-USER instead to avoid confusion.

    This engine is designed to read a story. It is not designed as an RPG
    engine. The story must be mostly linear, but can have branches. It is
    recommended that the branches converge simply for ease of writing. As of
    the current version, the engine cannot keep track of items or character
    state, but it is possible to do this within the story using branches.

What things you need to think about:

    story/ - this directory contains all story files and therefore the vast
             majority of the game.


What goes in story files?

The first line MUST be in the format of game-name,author,version.
For example, if Alice wrote version v3 of 'Hero Slayer', the first line
    would be Hero Slayer,Alice,v3
Note that spaces are allowed. Commas are not allowed except as delimiters

Every line after the first can be any one of the following:

Dialogue -  Just write the dialogue as you want it. No characters are handled
            by the engine, so you'll have to add those if you want.

Comments -  Preface a line with # and it'll be a comment.

End Game -  Preface the line with ! and the game ends there. Anything after
            that (including on the same line) is ignored.
